# Portfolio quality

This repo is a **Staff-level SDET portfolio artifact**. Technical correctness and interview narrative both matter.

## Strong signals in this codebase

- Feature-module test architecture with ADRs
- Layered test strategy (functional → integration → E2E → API → hybrid)
- Shared `pw-core` library and custom fixtures
- CI with typecheck, lint, credential gate, Playwright
- Docker support and documented test plan

## When adding work, ask

> Does this strengthen the story: "I design scalable test automation systems"?

Prefer:

- Clean boundaries and documented decisions
- Realistic OpenCart flows over trivial assertions
- Hybrid API/UI patterns where they demonstrate skill

Avoid:

- Flat spaghetti POM without feature ownership
- Tests that only duplicate existing coverage
- Complexity that cannot be explained in 60 seconds

## Interview mapping (examples)

| Artifact | Narrative |
| -------- | --------- |
| `src/features/` layers | Separation of concerns in test frameworks |
| `CatalogService` / `CartService` | API testability without UI coupling |
| `POMFixture` | Dependency injection for page objects |
| ADR-002 credentials | CI signal vs local ergonomics |
| `.github/agents/` | AI-assisted test engineering with guardrails |

## Documentation tie-in

Meaningful changes should update README, architecture docs, or ADRs so the portfolio stays self-explanatory.
